    "description": "Load every Python script on Python 3.9\n\n## Summary\n\nOn macOS, the `python3` that ships with the system is Python 3.9. Four crew scripts stopped at import on it, because their type hints use a form that Python 3.9 cannot read at run time. `crew-stats.py`, the script a person runs, was one of them. Now every script of the plugin loads and runs on Python 3.9, and the README states Python 3.9 as the lowest version a run needs.\n\nCloses #162\n\n**Ticket:** [Issue 162](https://github.com/jerridan/crew/issues/162)\n**Type:** Bug fix\n\n---\n\n## Agent context\n\n### Authority\n\n- `docs/design.md` §15 entry 51 (found the fault in `spend.py` and `crew-stats.py`) and the new §15 entry 144.\n- `.claude/rules/readme.md`: a new launch requirement goes in \"What a run needs\".\n\n### What changed, by file\n\n- `skills/project-lead/scripts/spend.py`, `crew-stats.py`, `crew-record.py`, `hooks/pre-compact.py`: each starts with `from __future__ import annotations`, so Python 3.9 stores each `X | None` annotation as text and does not evaluate it.\n- `README.md`: a \"Python 3.9 or newer\" row in \"What a run needs\".\n- `docs/design.md`: new §15 entry 144 that records the fault, the fix and the check.\n- `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`: version 0.1.111.\n\n### Constraints that applied\n\n- A change under `hooks/` and `skills/` bumps the version in both manifests. Both are 0.1.111.\n- No file of the concurrent orchestrator work (`launcher.py`, `crew-orch.py`, their tests, the orchestrator references) changed. `launcher.md` also says that `launcher.py` needs Python 3.9 or newer. It agrees with the README, so it stays as it is.\n\n### How this was verified\n\nOn `/usr/bin/python3` 3.9.6:\n- Every `.py` file of the plugin imports with no error. Before the change, `spend.py`, `crew-stats.py`, `crew-record.py` and `pre-compact.py` failed with `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for |: 'type' and 'NoneType'`. The one exception is `iterm2-tabs.py`: its `iterm2` package comes from `uv run --with iterm2` at run time. It parses on 3.9.\n- `crew-stats.py` reads the whole record root and exits 0. `crew-stats.py --help` exits 0.\n- `crew-record.py init` and `run state blocked` write a new record in a scratch directory.\n- `pre-compact.py` exits 0 on the payload `{}`.\n- A search for other features newer than 3.9 (`match`, `zip(strict=)`, `slots=True`, `tomllib` and similar) found none.\n\n### Known gaps\n\nNone\n",
